1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,538
This is StateGuard with a real Gmail connection. One approved test email has already been sent to the same account.

2
00:00:07,538 --> 00:00:14,879
We deliberately withheld its acknowledgment from the worker. This demonstration reuses that message. It does not

3
00:00:14,879 --> 00:00:21,040
send another email, and it does not pretend that the injected failure was a real Gmail outage.

4
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:28,698
We load the send attempt that was saved before the request. The worker belief is unknown, and retry is disabled.

5
00:00:28,698 --> 00:00:36,424
The durable claim prevents this demo from authorizing a second send, even after a restart. This is a conservative

6
00:00:36,424 --> 00:00:42,031
application safeguard, not a claim that Gmail itself offers exactly once delivery.

7
00:00:42,031 --> 00:00:50,002
The dashboard now queries Gmail. It finds one matching message with both Sent and Inbox labels. The result includes

8
00:00:50,002 --> 00:00:57,974
the time of the fresh check. Gmail rewrote our original Message ID, so the interface openly shows the fallback: the

9
00:00:57,974 --> 00:01:05,321
exact subject, sending account, and a narrow send window. That correlation is weaker and must be reviewed.

10
00:01:05,321 --> 00:01:13,012
Next, a real Strands agent investigates using OpenAI. One tool reads the saved send attempt and the injected

11
00:01:13,012 --> 00:01:21,059
acknowledgment loss. The other queries Gmail again. Only evidence for the approved test is returned, with mailbox

12
00:01:21,059 --> 00:01:28,964
addresses and message bodies excluded. The agent explains the evidence and recommends reconciliation. It has no

13
00:01:28,964 --> 00:01:31,171
send tool and no approval tool.

14
00:01:31,171 --> 00:01:38,696
The trace shows the actual tools called, their measured duration, and their returned evidence. The interface also

15
00:01:38,696 --> 00:01:46,355
reports model usage. This is the agent investigating the real Gmail test, not an archived replay. The deterministic

16
00:01:46,355 --> 00:01:52,681
recovery gate remains responsible for deciding whether the evidence is sufficient for approval.

17
00:01:52,681 --> 00:02:00,489
We approve reconciliation in the dashboard. The server rechecks Gmail and validates the decision version before

18
00:02:00,489 --> 00:02:08,579
updating local state. The worker now records delivered, recovery is complete, and retry remains disabled. The audit

19
00:02:08,579 --> 00:02:16,668
records the approval. Thirty five regression tests pass, including stale approvals and missing Inbox evidence. This

20
00:02:16,668 --> 00:02:24,405
proves one controlled self email recovery. Shared cloud storage and production reliability remain future work.